.TH geectl-request-add-review 1  "geectl-request-add-review 0.2.4" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-request\-add\-review \- Ask a user, group, project, or package to review a submit request
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl request add\-review\fR [\fB\-\-user\fR] [\fB\-\-group\fR] [\fB\-\-project\fR] [\fB\-\-package\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-comment\fR> <\fIID\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Ask a user, group, project, or package to review a submit request
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-user\fR \fI<USER>\fR
The user the review is asked of
.TP
\fB\-\-group\fR \fI<GROUP>\fR
The group the review is asked of
.TP
\fB\-\-project\fR \fI<PROJECT>\fR
The project the review is asked of
.TP
\fB\-\-package\fR \fI<PACKAGE>\fR
The package the review is asked of (needs its project)
.TP
\fB\-\-comment\fR \fI<COMMENT>\fR
The reason the review is asked for. Values starting with `\-` are taken literally: a comment may open with a `\- ` bullet
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIID\fR>
The request id
.SH VERSION
v0.2.4
